# Feature branches and registry

Do not create, implement, or commit feature work on `main`. `main` is merge-only.

## Before any product or spec work

1. Read `specifications/FEATURES.md`.
2. If the work has no row, add one first (next `CORE-NNN` or `AGENT-NNN`). Status `📋 Planned`, then `🔨 WorkInProgress` when implementation starts.
3. Create and switch to a branch from latest `origin/main`:

```text
CORE-012  →  feat/core-012
CORE-014  →  feat/core-014
AGENT-001 →  feat/agent-001
```

Pattern: `feat/<lowercase-feature-id>` (keep the zero padding).

```bash
git fetch origin
git checkout main
git pull
git checkout -b feat/core-014
```

## While working

- Keep the registry row in sync (status, assignee, plan/tasks links, notes).
- One feature id per branch. Do not pile unrelated fixes onto `feat/core-014`.
- Merge to `main` only through a reviewed PR (or an explicit human request to merge). After merge, mark the card `✅ Complete`.

## Do not

```text
❌ commit on main
❌ git checkout -b feat/fix / feat/agents / feat/mark-feature-complete
❌ start coding with no FEATURES.md row
❌ reuse an old feature branch for a new id
```
